    <span class="badge badge-teal">Executive Summary &amp; Submission Guide</span>
    <h1>DrivenData GEMS Submission Guide &amp; Nine-Site Executive Synthesis</h1>
    <p>Actionable, automated verification summary covering all 9 priority sites (<code>GEMSDOE24, 25, 27, 28, 30, 31, 32, 33, 36</code>), the wider peer ecosystem (<code>GEMSDOE..92</code>, <code>KANLER</code>, <code>WBG</code>, <code>karage</code>, <code>Apart</code>, <code>SASS</code>, <code>EUG</code>, <code>GINNY</code>), and exact instructions for <code>kanlergemsdoe3-h-k3s2-1-atsc-submod-exp-atsc-2-oof8f-37654-20261027-3108468e86b9-zeros</code>.</p>
    
    <div class="verdict-banner">
      <strong>AUTOMATED VERDICT: DO NOT SUBMIT TO COMPETITION &middot; RESEARCH-ONLY DOWNLOADS (ZERO HUMAN RASTER INSPECTION REQUIRED)</strong><br>
      1. <strong>Literal Fail-Closed Promotion Gate: <code>verdict = "negative"</code> (<code>slot_authorized = false</code>)</strong> — Against the registered <code>206,895</code>-dot <code>13GEMSDOE r13-lattice-s5</code> uniform grid probe covering <code>99.8713%</code> of the footprint within 3 px, <code>37,652 / 37,654</code> dots (<code>99.99%</code> unfiltered; <code>99.77%</code> off-catalogue-filtered; mathematical pigeonhole minimum <code>82.34%</code>) fall within 3 px. Under this repository's literal all-registry rule, a selector signature cannot waive or override a &gt;70% registry overlap.<br>
      2. <strong>Genuine Geological Detector Uniqueness (Scoped Diagnostic): PASS across all 87/87 real fault detectors</strong> in <code>GEMSDOE24..92</code>, <code>KANLERGEMSDOE1..3</code>, <code>WBGGEMSDOE1..3</code>, <code>GEMSDOEkarage1..3</code>, <code>ApartGEMSDOE1..3</code>, and <code>GEMSDOESASS1..3</code> (max 3-px dot overlap = <code>57.14% &le; 70%</code>; max |&rho;| = <code>0.0712 &le; 0.90</code>).<br>
      3. <strong>Scientific Spatial Holdout Gain: PASS (+66.4 bps Primary / +51.8 bps Orthogonal over Prior Repo Best)</strong> — <code>HOLDOUT-DTI = 0.163715</code> (95% CI <code>[0.153314, 0.174809]</code>, <code>60,988</code> withheld positives on participant-mirrored <code>gems-segment-pooled-v1</code>), outperforming prior repo best <code>CADG Exp-K3-3</code> (<code>0.157080</code>) and <code>B0_regional_d28</code> (<code>0.102255</code>, paired 95% CI <code>[+0.0488, +0.0740]</code>, <code>4/4</code> folds).<br>
      4. <strong>Local Saved-Byte Format Validation: PASS (16/16 checks on <code>finite-grid</code> and <code>template-mask</code>; Portal Acceptance Unverified)</strong> — Primary research file <code>kanlergemsdoe3-h-k3s2-1-atsc-submod-exp-atsc-2-oof8f-37654-20261027-3108468e86b9-zeros.tif</code> (SHA-256 <code>bf21ac69a0e5e6325d9725e7188be210a24b2e68b68060574db56af0d5972566</code>) is single-band <code>float32</code>, <code>EPSG:32611</code>, shape <code>(3730, 3292)</code>, with <strong>0 NaN / 0 Inf across all 12,279,160 whole-array pixels</strong> and exact values in <code>{0.0, 1.0}</code> (<code>37,654</code> off-catalogue dots, <code>0</code> catalogue overlap). Because the historically rejected upload was not supplied and template provenance is mirrored rather than organizer-signed, actual DrivenData portal acceptance remains unverified.<br>
      5. <strong>Fresh bounded final-dot audit (28 Oct): STOP.</strong> The exact saved bytes were compared with <code>249</code> selected current peer rasters (244 genuine detectors and 5 calibration/continuous probes). Final-dot overlap is <code>57.14%</code> versus genuine detectors but <code>100.00%</code> versus a continuous calibration probe. The bounded audit has no pre-placement surface or holdout result and cannot weaken the full-registry lattice stop.
    </div>
