        <small>Why emit both twins? Because the historically rejected upload that triggered <code>Error: Predicted values must be in range [0, 1]</code> was not supplied, its exact cause is unverified: an unmasked whole-array check fails on outside-footprint <code>NaN</code>, whereas a strict template-mask check expects <code>NaN</code> outside. We emit both <code>-zeros.tif</code> (<code>16/16</code> checks on <code>--profile finite-grid</code>; <code>0</code> NaN across all <code>12,279,160</code> cells) and <a download href="downloads/kanlergemsdoe3-h-k3s2-1-atsc-submod-exp-atsc-2-oof8f-37654-20261027-3108468e86b9-nan.tif"><code>-nan.tif</code></a> (<code>16/16</code> checks on <code>--profile template-mask</code>).</small>
      </li>
